.\" Man page for wordCount
.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "2026-09-24" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B #include \(dqmyfilefunctions.h\(dq
.PP
.BI "int wordCount(FILE *" file ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount()
function reads the file stream
.I file
from its current position until end of file, and counts its lines, words
and characters. The results are stored in the integers pointed to by
.IR lines ,
.I words
and
.IR chars .
.PP
Lines are counted as the number of newline characters. A word is a sequence
of characters separated by whitespace. Every byte read is counted as a
character. This matches the behaviour of
.BR wc (1).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success.
Returns \-1 if any argument is NULL.
.SH NOTES
After this function returns, the file position is at end of file. Call
.BR rewind (3)
before reading the file again.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mygrep (3),
.BR wc (1)
